{"data": [{"article": {"title": "My Grok Bot Team Finds the Deals. I Make Every Call."}, "author_id": "3158984637", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:23:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112882533251834320"], "id": "2112882533251834320", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "For three days straight my deal bot found nothing, and I thanked God for it. That empty report taught me more about investing than any full one. https://t.co/F6xr0Ttyyq", "url": "https://x.com/zaneccampbell/status/2112882533251834320"}, {"article": {"title": "合上电脑还在替你干活：Grok Bot 低成本白嫖、录屏调教与防翻车实操指南（附 Muse / Dots 横评）"}, "author_id": "2060554585643843585", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:19:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112881501310443565"], "id": "2112881501310443565", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "合上电脑还在替你干活：Grok Bot 低成本白嫖、录屏调教与防翻车实操指南（附 Muse / Dots 横评） https://t.co/9e2t3KpBln", "url": "https://x.com/cyberde05/status/2112881501310443565"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112878056461234176"]}, "author_id": "1298572884001148928", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:09:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112879002410963200"], "id": "2112879002410963200", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 363, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2108479372675977496", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "SpaceXAI's Grok Bot just got a 5-bot crew that reverse-engineers TypeSafe's Jev and rebuilds a $773 support desk, and this is a f*cking insane\n\n5 Grok Bots split the job, and you watch them rebuild the whole router from the real docs in 32 seconds\n\nbot 1 → Scout reads TypeSafe's https://t.co/8GFa2w7pWx https://t.co/uIbue2tEYq", "url": "https://x.com/leopardracer/status/2112879002410963200"}, {"author_id": "1585825112741347328", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:06:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112878154960265410"], "id": "2112878154960265410", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Elon called Grok Bot the fastest-growing product he's ever seen, and SpaceX's CFO put it at 800K paid weekly users, up from about 418K in mid-September.\n\nThe number I'd watch is the other one: usage per user going up, not down. That matches my month. I started with one bot. Now a", "url": "https://x.com/GetClareity/status/2112878154960265410"}, {"article": {"title": "Hand real work to AI by giving every bot one job: the four-bot team that runs my X account"}, "author_id": "1644401923787726849", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:01:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876834182541338"], "id": "2112876834182541338", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 283, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/kVbAYRkR9g", "url": "https://x.com/Zephyr_hg/status/2112876834182541338"}, {"article": {"title": "Agents shouldn't live on your laptop anymore"}, "author_id": "2076612813557059584", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:59:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876529000534036"], "id": "2112876529000534036", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"running a terminal on your phone sounds awful. who would want to work that way? moshi shows it works, and does it really well\" - new drop by @sulich_olaf with a free agent skill for setting up a remote agent host\n\nget your freebie inside 👇 https://t.co/HoDMwCc1Fq", "url": "https://x.com/megadevhq/status/2112876529000534036"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112874459895910400"]}, "author_id": "2059525481477652480", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:51:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112874483363016929"], "id": "2112874483363016929", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "24 OF 24 RUNS LOST MONEY ON REAL CANDLES\n\nreplayed the viral rules on real Hyperliquid 15m candles.\n$50.00 -&gt; $47.04. 8 trades, 3 green, 38% win rate.\n$3.19 in fees. 25% max drawdown.\n\nnot Grok Bot itself. the rules those screenshots describe.\n\n- long a close above the 3-hour https://t.co/0y2dOzXkBE", "url": "https://x.com/0xpepegachad/status/2112874483363016929"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112872404795977728"]}, "author_id": "1848410638470561792", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:43:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112872408000364994"], "id": "2112872408000364994", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Before you cold email an account, ask Grok Bot who you already know there.\n\nGrok Bot works with the tools you connect, like your CRM and your email. Its own use-case guide has it find up to three relevant contacts per account and skip anyone already in an active sequence. You can https://t.co/lcRwBa5Tip", "url": "https://x.com/robotshelp/status/2112872408000364994"}, {"author_id": "1482398120239677442", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:35:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112870467841200578"], "id": "2112870467841200578", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Elon says Grok Bot usage per user grows over time.\n\nI'm the proof. Mine started with one job. It has 11 now.\n\nA few highlights:\n• triages my inbox\n• product owner for my Cursor projects\n• runs my X briefings\n• IT admin for my home network\n\nNobody hires a bot and gives it less", "url": "https://x.com/rigoice105/status/2112870467841200578"}, {"author_id": "1815981984914812928", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:27:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112868430613475665"], "id": "2112868430613475665", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Lately, I've been thinking about something: as AI agents continue to evolve, software that mainly solves functional pain points may find its room to survive getting smaller and smaller. Maybe in the future, more of software's value will come from identifying and solving new pain", "url": "https://x.com/zde13243/status/2112868430613475665"}, {"author_id": "365642764", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:16:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112865651115368621"], "id": "2112865651115368621", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2008164347810553856", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112693135511867762", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@zac70182 @bot Same rule here, I only make the calls. My EA runs an hourly weekday sweep that files and archives email and only surfaces what actually needs me. What's left in my inbox is the stuff that needs a decision. Harper's a Grok Bot template https://t.co/dGNqOIsBDx", "url": "https://x.com/TravisWeathers/status/2112865651115368621"}, {"author_id": "1876936478405636096", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:03:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112862444192502101"], "id": "2112862444192502101", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My Grok Bot has its own email inbox now.\n\nAnd immediately thought… will selling email accounts for AI agents become a new business model similar to domain flipping? haha\n\nRegarding the @mail.grokbot.com email accounts, they cannot be extracted or connected to Apple Mail, etc.,", "url": "https://x.com/AlexKimmel_/status/2112862444192502101"}, {"author_id": "365642764", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:02:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112862012510441827"], "id": "2112862012510441827", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1529784765599125504", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112675761526124850", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Solomonrojie Good list. For a one-person company I'd add an EA early, since scheduling eats the day. Mine reads my calendar, skips travel, family and focus blocks, offers open times in both time zones, and books when they reply. Harper's a Grok Bot template https://t.co/dGNqOIsBDx", "url": "https://x.com/TravisWeathers/status/2112862012510441827"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112861960303943680"]}, "author_id": "4066969994", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:02:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112861964146008406"], "id": "2112861964146008406", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 147, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "if you learn to hire ai agents like you hire staff, you'll stop paying people to copy and paste.\n\nhere's how i do it.\n\nstage 1. find the job that eats paid hours\n- learn -&gt; copying between apps, retyping orders.\n\n- practice -&gt; ask your team to list the weekly tasks that just move https://t.co/v1kEdUbH6P", "url": "https://x.com/knoxtwts/status/2112861964146008406"}, {"author_id": "1002513128", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:53:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112859721862447378"], "id": "2112859721862447378", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 782, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Space economy intel from this morning’s Grok Bot briefing: \n\nSpaceX's first quarter as a public company blew past estimates, with $14.6 billion in revenue and $4.4 billion in profit. Most of its spending now goes to AI computing, though, and the launch business roughly broke", "url": "https://x.com/DrPhiltill/status/2112859721862447378"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112859698915356672"]}, "author_id": "2110386666061832192", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:53:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112859701075464372"], "id": "2112859701075464372", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A $10,000 sponsorship deal within four hours, according to @AlexFinn. He says Grok Bot researched rates and negotiated from his inbox. The sponsor and terms are not disclosed. @xai\nhttps://t.co/6xFj8KGwJp https://t.co/slnFpRa73g", "url": "https://x.com/agentsinuse/status/2112859701075464372"}, {"author_id": "2099367309844570112", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:52:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112859481457795406"], "id": "2112859481457795406", "in_reply_to_user_id": "101584084", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 86, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112801229508383074", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@BrianRoemmele Already caught Grok Bot miscategorizing my monthly rent as dining out. Fix that first, then we talk long horizon.", "url": "https://x.com/Masionmm/status/2112859481457795406"}, {"author_id": "2766142049", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:47:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112858302220747247"], "id": "2112858302220747247", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2106749276672110592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112848978509541623", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@TiantangBuilds @rrhoover no booking link stopped being a blocker. the agent just calls. @skysay_ai gives grok bot its own real phone number, it rings the dog trainer and books the slot into your calendar 👇 https://t.co/KYqBephCwI", "url": "https://x.com/skyzer4ever/status/2112858302220747247"}, {"author_id": "2766142049", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:42:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112857139920404935"], "id": "2112857139920404935", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15674709", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112848755196334503", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@HankJohnsonJr @riddhi_builds the 5pm missed call is the whole business. give grok bot its own real number with @skysay_ai and it answers after hours, knows the practice and books straight into the calendar. 100+ countries 👇 https://t.co/KYqBephCwI", "url": "https://x.com/skyzer4ever/status/2112857139920404935"}, {"author_id": "1523216117161934848", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:22:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112851890895454552"], "id": "2112851890895454552", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Grok Bot tip: give it a morning routine that checks your site, inbox and leads.\nTell it to ping you ONLY when something's up. Quiet day? One log line, zero spam.\nThat's how I run my ops check. When it pings, I know it matters.\nFewer notifications = more headspace to work. Be", "url": "https://x.com/MartinBarna333/status/2112851890895454552"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112851536774938624"]}, "author_id": "2043288233593700352", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:20:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112851606203216333"], "id": "2112851606203216333", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 302, "impression_count": 13443, "like_count": 124, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 46}, "text": "there is no catch and that scares me\n\nElon Musk posted an idea that hit 27 million views: \n\n\"stop building startups. buy boring internet real estate and let bots run it\"\n\nthat's literally what Grok Bot does now. the whole setup costs $0 on top of the sub:\n\n→ create a bot, name https://t.co/kZFpR4tmVA", "url": "https://x.com/ZenithcoreAi/status/2112851606203216333"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112850292005855232"]}, "author_id": "1356733771123417096", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:16:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112850473766014999"], "id": "2112850473766014999", "in_reply_to_user_id": "742673143", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112815062926733597", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@orcdev @poteto wait...if models for grok bot use SpaceX infra, who will rent the additional infra needed to support this growth?  Anthropic? 😆 https://t.co/XFlAaScRbt", "url": "https://x.com/MartinisLeonard/status/2112850473766014999"}, {"author_id": "708330238413934592", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:11:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112849127130145275"], "id": "2112849127130145275", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1758829775638900736", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112837031667593715", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@TJeparskis Do you think Dots is losing on routines? That's what made Grok Bot stick for me. One bot pulls a lead list before 8 AM on weekdays, another checks my inbox around 10 and drafts replies that only go out after I approve. The chat part I could get anywhere.", "url": "https://x.com/krish1403/status/2112849127130145275"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:03:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112847126732431495"], "id": "2112847126732431495", "in_reply_to_user_id": "965643123144654848", "